    <bpmn:process id="W_W3883" name="W3883. Customer Identity Resolution &amp; Profile Stitching" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ingestion (W3882); new identifier
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~600K loyalty + ~515K ecommerce customers/yr + cash walk-ins; identity graph maintained
Owner: CDP / Data Science
Participants: CDP Team, Data Science (links to VS-30.2), Data Engineering (links to VS-28/VS-27), Loyalty (links to VS-13), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), Trade (links to VS-11/VS-16), Privacy (links to VS-91), Fraud (links to VS-125/W3861)
Source: workflow W3883 — Customer Identity Resolution &amp; Profile Stitching</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3883_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3883_Lane1" name="CDP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3883_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3883_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3883_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3883_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3883_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3883_Start3" name="Ingestion (W3882); new identifier">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3883_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3883_Task4" name="CDP/Data Science build identity resolution: deterministic matching on verified…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CDP/Data Science build identity resolution: deterministic matching on verified identifiers (loyalty ID, email, phone, trade account, card token) and probabilistic matching on device/behavior/name/address for anonymous-to-known stitching (links to VS-125 device graph for fraud), with confidence scoring and survivorship rules
Responsible (R): CDP / Data Science
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3883_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3883_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3883_Task5" name="CDP stitch profiles into the resolved identity graph, surface duplicate/split…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CDP stitch profiles into the resolved identity graph, surface duplicate/split identities for review, and handle household/B2B-account-group resolution (links to VS-107 key account hierarchy)
Responsible (R): CDP / Data Science
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3883_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3883_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3883_Task6" name="CDP/Privacy ensure resolution complies with RA 10173 (lawful basis, no unlawful…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CDP/Privacy ensure resolution complies with RA 10173 (lawful basis, no unlawful re-identification of anonymized data, cross-entity sharing limits — links to VS-91/VS-72) and document the resolution logic for DSAR response (links to W3900)
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3883_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3883_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3883_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3883_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3883_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-607 (ensure controlled execution — CDP Architecture, Ingestion &amp; Identity Resolution (PA-126.1).) | - operational: confidence thresholds and survivorship rules; operational: deterministic-first matching
Owner: CDP / Data Science</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
