    <bpmn:process id="W_W3884" name="W3884. Customer Golden Record &amp; Master Profile Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Resolution (W3883); profile update
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: ~600K–1M+ resolved customer profiles
Owner: CDP / Data Governance
Participants: CDP Team, Data Governance (links to VS-29/VS-28.2), Loyalty (links to VS-13), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), Trade (links to VS-11/VS-16), Marketing (links to VS-14), Privacy (links to VS-91), Insights (links to VS-28.1)
Source: workflow W3884 — Customer Golden Record &amp; Master Profile Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3884_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3884_Lane1" name="CDP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3884_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3884_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3884_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3884_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3884_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3884_Start3" name="Resolution (W3883); profile update">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3884_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3884_Task4" name="CDP/Data-Governance define and maintain the golden customer record: the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CDP/Data-Governance define and maintain the golden customer record: the canonical attributes (identity, contact, preferences, segments, CLV, lifecycle stage, consent), survivorship rules across sources (which source wins for each attribute), and the relationship to the foundational customer master (links to VS-29)
Responsible (R): CDP / Data Governance
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
