        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CDP run periodic hygiene: bounce/engagement suppressions for marketing (links to VS-14), deceased/do-not-contact handling, returned-mail/invalid-address cleanup, and trade-account verification refresh (links to VS-16/VS-86 KYB)
Responsible (R): CDP / Marketing / Trade
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3886_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3886_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3886_Task6" name="CDP triage and remediate DQ issues (links to VS-27 W734 data-quality triage)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CDP triage and remediate DQ issues (links to VS-27 W734 data-quality triage), route source-system fixes to source owners (links to VS-29), and report DQ KPIs (validity %, duplicate rate)
Responsible (R): CDP / Data Governance
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3886_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3886_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
